{"title":"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Interesting_note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Interesting note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Patrick started walking at a constant speed along a straight road from his school to the park. One hour after Patrick left, Tanya started running at a constant speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour faster than Patrick walked, following the same straight road from the school to the park. One hour after Tanya left, Jose started bicycling at a constant speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour faster than Tanya ran, following the same straight road from the school to the park. All three people arrived at the park at the same time. The distance from the school to the park is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> miles, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We set up the equation in units of time, with Patrick's speed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and the distance to the park as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254c0810f8ea4bcd61092920be28168edba0191d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s} = \\frac{d}{s+2} + 1 = \\frac{d}{s+9} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"214\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>From the first two expressions, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/956bb3d81a808efed1789069486489e9d4cf6d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ds + 2d = sd - s^2 - 2s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />. From the first and third expressions, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5cdc0d321390b6a85e7f6bba67187222864e28d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ds + 9d = sd - s^2 - 9s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>After solving this system of equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561fb54fea7a9cdac0efd8deac154c457b2feec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{252}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4dd378f901b7e795f3ffb3890892e0b4593c2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{277}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logibyte\" title=\"Logibyte\">Logibyte</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Patrick's speed be R and his time spent walking to the part be T. Let the distance of his school to the park be D. So, we can write the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaedbb902958cf47c9ae0570f832f2dd5ff87926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=RT.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> After going through the problem, we can write that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1816bd6629a0410cfb6a69ad5ac531d4de5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(R+2)(T-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6bab8148991c5c6e75c0e395fc68b92b8da1b254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(R+9)(T-2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> We can substitute the last two equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f517e2f8866f1d7c15aa21f4d3f108f77f2603.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(R+2)(T-1)=(R+9)(T-2)\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/22822045442ac5ee0cee483678ca9e27a63d5025.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[RT+2T-R-2=RT+9T-2R-18.\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"14\" /> Simplifying this, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfeb553efb4dfbb3855da56a60a829e7f380d963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=7T-16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> We can plug the two equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b5548d6919e956b1edf9ddf9392b7fdde6563149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=RT$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d1816bd6629a0410cfb6a69ad5ac531d4de5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(R+2)(T-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510c96f2381b276dec0917cb772ea9460e1e27ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[RT=RT+2T-R-2.\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"14\" /> We can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594dddd733207ea03b10d1eda35a7823ce9ec76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=7T-16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5decb150f4771a2e78ee04a480ee11e988ba03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(7T-16)T=(7T-16)T+2T-(7T-16)-2.\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"18\" /> Simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e14d00a58695959553ccaa3e237f46a795ee50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5T=14\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/43547cf110874fd93465b7fb8960263d5e41cf54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=\\frac{14}{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> We can now find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5318aa9f62eab79cc88673414583ae797303da36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=7\\left(\\frac{14}{5} \\right)-16=\\frac{18}{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"192\" height=\"45\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fab64a2dab75aa00ac22c412557d461b2127732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=RT,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d53e728779eb4370e0d8c2defb4c94d4c91dfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\frac{18}{5} \\cdot \\frac{14}{5}=\\frac{252}{25}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" /> That means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/385bdd47e0384889bbbb10a4398e26a6cc1f73ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{277}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~gogogo2022\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Faraz's speed be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Tanya runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mph faster, and Jose bikes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mph faster.\n</p><p>Faraz walks for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour before Tanya starts, creating a gap of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> miles. Since Tanya gains on him at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mph, the time it takes her to catch Faraz is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffd5cbe261ac04cfe666a8a6c302943b88f62d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{p}{2}\\]\" width=\"10\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>Tanya then runs for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour before Jose starts, creating a gap of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b23df32b73d64aff7b86e3ffc72cf19e94f54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> miles. Jose gains on her at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mph, so the time it takes him to catch Tanya is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/5651b14cfb445c6080a1e51dbd98624ecaa725c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{p+2}{7}\\]\" width=\"41\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since they arrive at the park at the same time and Jose started <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour later,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe623128065a025311924cf1011589e2f52ad4f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{p}{2} - \\frac{p+2}{7} = 1\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Solving,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67fea02d8c8c57bde16c88928ab5ab758edcea2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 7p - 2(p+2) &amp;= 14 \\\\ 5p &amp;= 18 \\\\ p &amp;= \\frac{18}{5} \\end{align*}\" width=\"148\" height=\"87\" />\n</p><p>Faraz's total travel time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8ecdda0e6f50aeeb8fe99232815909a2238192d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{2}+1=\\frac{14}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> hours, so the distance is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22eaf9db32f446c5dc6a28bab1a66f082d3b2fc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D = \\frac{18}{5}\\cdot\\frac{14}{5}=\\frac{252}{25}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52ed949091f09dbb38e6a1a2922400ab72811eaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m+n=\\boxed{277}.\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~matchas (Made by a ninth grader if any issues feel free to edit!)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Interesting_note\">Interesting note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Interesting note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is identical to the 2020 Purple Comet Middle School #8:\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://purplecomet.org/views/data/2020MSSolutions.pdf\">https://purplecomet.org/views/data/2020MSSolutions.pdf</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy_.F0.9F.94.A5.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J96-4l0i7T4\">2026 AIME I #1</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://piacademyus.org/\">piacademyus.org</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\">Video Solution (Similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sNd5zkIMgHM\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sNd5zkIMgHM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Intuitive)\">Video Solution (Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=twFpo62THNA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=twFpo62THNA</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YhvQwyhQAlw\">https://youtu.be/YhvQwyhQAlw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsecti